A||N||44||AusFiero||My doctor rang me a home ...things are not good||||9||
Z||000000||AusFiero||06-29-2001||05:11 AM||||Ok this isn't Fiero related but most people I talk to a lot post in this section.<P>I went for an EEC brain scan today and instead of the usual week for results my doctor rang me at home hours later.<P>Seems my illness is no mystery anymore as I have a Cyst on my brain  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Understandably I am i shock at the moment and really worried.<P>They tell me it is benign but I have to go to the doctors Monday for immediate referal to a specialist in the brain field for surgery ASAP. I dont fancy part of my skull being removed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I can't swear on here but I guess you know how I feel right now<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||9
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-29-2001||05:53 AM||||Best of luck to you. Modern medicine has now made this type of surgery pretty commonplace. Anytime you have any surgery is a little bit of risk. Ive even heard of brain surgery done and patient going home in a couple of days. Again,hope the best to you.<P>on a lite note, people have told me for years I needed brain surgery too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||06-29-2001||05:58 AM||||At least you know know what your problems has been in the past.  This actually might be good news.  Hopefully it will be easy to remove or treat.  I work for a hospital and can tell you that these type of procedures are becomming very common.  Depends on where the cyst is at.<BR>Once removed or shrunk, since its non cancerous, you should make a full recovery, and be back to making us all kinds of cool fiero stuff.. Just make sure you get several opinions from different doctors.  Then do some research yourself..  The more you know the better.<P>Ross<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 06-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||beachbomb||06-29-2001||05:59 AM||||My prayers are with you! Try not to worry and always think positive! Everything will turn out okay....take care Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||10
Z||000004||grinthock||06-29-2001||07:04 AM||||My prayers are with you dude, just an FYI, there are 2 types of surgery that (well at least here in canada) are now a FINE science and have been almost perfected, one is Heart Surgury and the other is Brain Surgury (Well Canadians DID find the cure for epilepsy!! {{Anyone smell burnt toast?}})<P>Don't sweat it, you have a long road ahead with your surgury and recovery but you will be fine..... Take it easy, my mother is a Oncologist (Cancer Thearpist) and is involved with studies and research, after speaking with her she mentioned you have NOTHING to worry about.||||reg||1
